Z||000000||Adrift||12-18-2001||09:37 PM||||Look what happened to my new, rebuilt caliper? How do I go about fixing this? Is there any trick to it or do I just try to compress the spring while screwing the piston down?<P>Thanks<BR>Ari<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DCP_1666.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||avengador1||12-18-2001||10:44 PM||||When I rebuilt mine. I used a pair of channel lock pliers and a piece of wood to compress it. Be carefull to not nick the new seal when you reassemble it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||ka4nkf||12-18-2001||11:34 PM||||I think I would return it for another one.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Adrift||12-18-2001||11:44 PM||||Can you return it because that happens?||||reg||1
Z||000004||DKOV||12-18-2001||11:50 PM||||Return it man... that aint right.<P>If memory serves, there is some kind of retainer that is supposed to keep that from just popping out like that.  They DO come all the way out, but it should FALL out...<P>I'd return it rather than fix it.  Think of it this way, if you don't do it exactly right and it fails on the street, YOU are responcible for its failure, NOT the factory.<P>By getting them to fix it, you absolve yourself and provide your future recourse if needed.<P>JMHO<P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000005||Neal||12-19-2001||01:25 AM||||Dont bother returning it, inspect everything against a blow-up diagram.  If it all looks right keep it.  It is as simple as screwing the piston back into the caliper, but much easier said than done...<P>there is a trick to it but id rebuilt mine to long ago... well on second thought if you dont wanna fight with it get the exchange...<P>Hmmm not to sound like a dick but the other day you asked about jack points on the car and now your being phased by a piston popping out, well are you sure about trusting yourself to brake work?||||reg||1
Z||000006||GTDude||12-19-2001||08:49 AM||||Make your life easy dude....just get another one.  It's not all that easy to get it back in.  Can be done...but why aggravate yourself.  Get a new one and be happy!  Merry Xmas.<P>phil pettus<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DSCF0003a_3.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
